body:
The maintainer decided on 2026-11-22 (question dialog), with the option "Targeted tests, heavy at the cut". His words: "Why are we doing heavy builds locally at all? should be small targeted shallow tests".

## Why
The rule "Heavy lanes at review" (#2568, with #3460, #3467 and #3470) asks for a heavy run of 200 to 260 steps for each PR whose diff reaches a heavy lane. One run takes 50 to 140 minutes and one release build tree. On 2026-11-22 the machine merged 7 PRs in 3 hours for this reason.

## The new rule
1. At review a PR needs only:
   - its own pinning tests;
   - the touched test binaries (the quick plan);
   - the example catalog suites by name, where a post or a toolpath changed (#3521);
   - the light lane (`cargo xtask gate light`).
2. No full heavy lane for each PR. A diff that reaches a heavy lane is not "not ready" for that reason. No PR is "owed heavy".
3. The full heavy lanes run only at the cut (the release tier on the cut runner) and on the post-merge and cut runners.
4. A `P1` PR under the safety floor gets one targeted heavy step: the named heavy tests of the changed code. `P2` and lower get none.
5. The heavy lock (`.claude/heavy-run.lock`) stays for the targeted step.
6. `cargo xtask gate heavy` and its flag `--covers` stay as commands. They are not a condition for "ready" or for a merge.

## Work (one PR, text only, no code)
Change the text that cites #2568, #3460, #3467 or #3470 in:
- `AGENTS.md`: "Heavy lanes at review", "The light lane", and the Pull Request Law where it names heavy results;
- `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md`;
- `.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md`;
- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md` and the agent file of the PR reviewer if it names heavy lanes;
- `.claude/skills/merge-ready/SKILL.md` (step 4a, the wave form: keep the command, remove it from the merge condition);
- `.claude/skills/classify-effort/SKILL.md`.

The PR body has `Process change: yes`. A decision file records the rule and what was dropped.

## Related
- #3513, #3514, #3515: slow tests of the quick and batch plans.
- The selection of the quick plan (the next issue, linked below).

Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q05 (40 x 40 x 100 block on a Tormach 770MX + microARC 4), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release; reproduced by hand.

## What happens

```
import_model {"name": "q05-4axis", "path": ".../q05-4axis.step"}
load_machine {"builtin": "Tormach 770MX + microARC 4"}
set_stock {"axis": "x", "box": {"dx": 44, "dy": 44, "dz": 110}}
add_tool {"catalog": "DR-0600", "name": "6mm Drill"}
add_setup {"name": "Setup1"}; add_setup {"name": "Setup2", "datum_from": "Setup1"}
lay_part_on_face {"setup": "Setup2", "face": {"model": "q05-4axis", "id": "face:0x9a06666bad6a627f"}, "plane": "g17", "place": false}   -> "turned X -90°"
add_operation {"kind": "drill", "name": "D", "source": "q05-4axis", "tool": "6mm Drill"}
detect_holes {"name": "D"}   -> {"holes": 2, "radial_holes": 1, "skipped": [], "undersize": []}
generate {"name": "D"}       -> D: invalid machining parameters: this op lists Z holes AND cross holes - drill either the mill's holes or the turret's, not both (M5.2 v1)
edit_operation {"name": "D", "params": {"cross": []}}   -> bad params patch: unknown field cross - a drill operation has no field "cross"; see list_operation_types
```

The "radial hole" is the Ø20 x 2 mm counterbore on the face that points down in this setup (`dir [0,0,1], origin [50,0,-20], radius 10`). It goes into `params.drill.cross`, a list for live-tooling cross holes on a turret, on a machine that has no turret. `undersize` stays empty although Ø20 > the Ø6 drill. `cross` is not in list_operation_types and edit_operation refuses it, so the operation can only be deleted and its holes typed in by hand.

## Expected

On a mill, `detect_holes` keeps only the holes the tool can reach along the setup's Z (here the two Ø6 front holes) and names the others in `skipped`; any list it fills can be edited or cleared through edit_operation.

## Repro files

[q05-4axis.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/q05-4axis.step); agent report [REPORT.md](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/REPORT.md) problem 3. Related: #2601 (opposite radial holes merged).

Done means: the steps above give a Drill op with the 2 front holes and the counterbore in `skipped`, and it generates (pinned by a test); `cross` is either editable or never filled on a machine without a turret.
